// f32 `sin`, `cos` and `tan`, ported from LLVM libc into `core::libm`, against LLVM libc itself. For each
// input, given by its bits, this prints the bits of the 3 results (a NaN as 2143289344). The
// expected line is what LLVM libc at f475f085bf7b prints, built with FMA. The inputs are every input LLVM libc special-cases or lists as an exception and every boundary between the code's branches, each with its two neighbours and both signs; an input reaching each entry of the 64-entry table; inputs in every regime of the range reduction, up to the largest float; zeros, infinities, quiet and signaling NaNs and subnormals. The port was
// also checked against LLVM libc on all 2^32 inputs.
//
